      "rule": "R11",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "The `no_table_exists` mutant looks for the `.table` case followed directly by the `.index` case in `Resolution/Definitions.lean`. This commit inserts a `.viewExists` case between them, so the text count is not 1 and the mutant run fails (`text.count(before) != 1` at line 144). Fix: update the `before` and `after` text to include the new `.view` case, and run the touched mutant by name."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261024T214759Z-59dc5215#2",
      "line": 64,
      "path": "conformance/resolve_mutants.py",
      "rule": "R11",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "The `no_such_table` mutant looks for `| none => prepareError catalog (.noSuchTable tableName)` in `Resolution/AddColumn.lean`. That line is now a two-line `if (catalog.findView …) … else …` expression, so the match fails. Fix: rewrite the mutant against the new `| none =>` form and run it by name."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261024T214759Z-59dc5215#3",
      "line": 22,
      "path": "conformance/drop_mutants.py",
      "rule": "R11",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "The `if_exists_reports_missing` mutant looks for the one-line `| none => if ifExists then … else prepareError catalog (.noSuchTable name)` in `Resolution/Drops.lean`. This commit splits it into a view-restriction branch plus an `else if ifExists …` branch, so the match fails. Fix: update the mutant text to the new two-line form and run it by name."
